      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SIGN OF THE TIMES (7) is the one to beat off a sound Bunbury debut, where he was third in a Mdn on soft ground after racing keenly and being bumped at straightening. That race experience, barrier one and an easy Albany trial win two weeks ago give him the most appealing profile in a race that looks to have a long tail. LUZ DEL SOL (8) won a recent trial at this track in readiness after tackling an Open 2YO race before the break. She's been handy in maiden company around some efforts in Saturday grade. Drawn well here and can play a leading role. DUNDEEMICKY (3) brings no race form to assess, though first-time blinkers and a family with 1000m winners give him some debut interest. GOD'LL GETYA (1) was second at this track before the break despite racing wide throughout, and the 3kg claim helps his place claims if he brings that trial form to raceday. BLINDING LUCK (4) is next best.",
